These are input scripts for benchmarking many of the interatomic
potentials in LAMMPS.  Each input runs 100 MD steps for a system of
about 32,000 atoms (16,000 for SNAP).  The inputs were used to compare
the computational cost of the potentials in the LAMMPS paper:

  A. P. Thompson et al., Comp Phys Comm, 271, 108171 (2022)

The "Benchmarks" section of the LAMMPS manual lists the number of
floating-point operations per atom and timestep for most of them
(https://docs.lammps.org/Speed_bench.html).

Any potential parameter files used by the input scripts are also
included in this directory.  The inputs need LAMMPS to be compiled
with the following packages:

  in.adp       MANYBODY
  in.airebo    MANYBODY
  in.bop       MANYBODY
  in.comb      MANYBODY
  in.dpd       DPD-BASIC
  in.eam       MANYBODY
  in.eff       EFF
  in.eim       MANYBODY
  in.fene      MOLECULE
  in.gb        ASPHERE
  in.granular  GRANULAR
  in.lj        (none)
  in.meam      MEAM
  in.peri      PERI
  in.protein   KSPACE, MOLECULE, RIGID
  in.reaxff    REAXFF
  in.rebo      MANYBODY
  in.snap      ML-SNAP
  in.spce      KSPACE, MOLECULE, RIGID
  in.sw        MANYBODY
  in.tersoff   MANYBODY

Examples of how to run these scripts on one or four CPU cores:

  lmp -in in.fene
  mpirun -np 4 lmp -in in.protein

The CPU time (in seconds) for the run is in the "Loop time" line of
the log files.  The log files in this directory were created with one
MPI process and one OpenMP thread pinned to one core of an otherwise
idle machine, with LAMMPS (development version 30 Sep 2026, commit
8e29ee3d8c) compiled by GCC using the cmake/presets/gcc.cmake preset,
the default build type (-O2) for generic x86_64 CPUs
(-march=x86-64 -mtune=generic), and the KISS FFT library, e.g.:

  lmp -in in.fene -log log.4Nov2026.fene.AMD-Zen4

The suffix of the log file name indicates the CPU:

  AMD-Zen4    AMD Ryzen Threadripper PRO 7985WX (Zen 4), 64 cores,
              3.2 GHz base clock, run at 3.15 GHz (boost off),
              128 GB DDR5-4800 memory in 4 channels,
              Fedora Linux 44, GCC 16.2.1, MPICH 4.2.2

  Intel-BDW   2x Intel Xeon E5-2620 v4 (Broadwell), 2x 8 cores,
              2.1 GHz base clock, run at 3.0 GHz (turbo),
              512 GB DDR4-2133 memory in 2x 4 channels,
              Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS, GCC 15.2.0, Open MPI 5.0.10

  Intel-Casc  2x Intel Xeon Gold 6248 (Cascade Lake), 2x 20 cores,
              2.5 GHz base clock, run at 3.2 GHz (turbo),
              384 GB DDR4-2933 memory in 2x 6 channels,
              Rocky Linux 10.2, GCC 14.3.1, MPICH 4.1.2
